# InvoiceMe Project Rules

## Architecture Principles

### Domain-Driven Design (DDD)
- Domain entities (Customer, Invoice, Payment) are aggregate roots
- Business logic belongs in domain entities, not in handlers or controllers
- Value objects (Email, Address, Money, IDs) are immutable
- Repository interfaces defined in domain layer, implementations in infrastructure

### Command Query Responsibility Segregation (CQRS)
- Commands (write operations) return void or acknowledgment
- Queries (read operations) return data only, never modify state
- Separate command and query handlers in different vertical slices
- Commands: createCustomer/, updateCustomer/, deleteCustomer/, createInvoice/, etc.
- Queries: getCustomer/, listCustomers/, getInvoice/, listInvoices/, etc.

### Vertical Slice Architecture (VSA)
- Organize code by features/use cases, not technical layers
- Each feature contains: Controller, Handler, Command/Query, DTO
- Feature location: `backend/src/main/java/com/invoiceme/features/`
- Example structure: `features/customers/createCustomer/` contains all components for that feature

## Code Organization

### Backend Structure
```
domain/          # Pure business logic, no framework dependencies
features/        # Vertical slices (CQRS commands/queries)
infrastructure/ # Framework implementations (JPA, Security)
shared/          # Cross-cutting concerns (exceptions, mappers)
config/          # Application configuration
```

### Frontend Structure (MVVM)
```
types/          # TypeScript type definitions
services/       # API communication layer
viewmodels/     # Presentation logic (MVVM pattern)
components/     # React UI components
app/            # Next.js App Router pages
```

## Key Patterns

### Money Object Handling
- Backend sends monetary values as `{amount: number, currency: string}` objects
- Frontend must extract `.amount` and `.currency` properties for display
- Never assume Money is a number - always access object properties

### Form Validation
- Backend: Jakarta Bean Validation on all DTOs
- Frontend: Client-side validation in ViewModels with backend error mapping
- Validation includes field-level (required, format) and business rules (date ranges, payment amounts)

### Error Handling
- Backend: GlobalExceptionHandler with consistent error responses
- Frontend: Error handling in ViewModels with user-friendly messages
- Validation errors include field-level details via ValidationErrorResponse

### Authentication
- JWT-based stateless authentication
- Token stored in localStorage, auto-attached to requests via axios interceptors
- Protected routes use ProtectedRoute wrapper component
- Default admin: username `admin`, password `admin123` (change in production!)

## Testing Requirements
- Domain logic: Unit tests in domain layer
- Integration tests: End-to-end workflows
- All tests must pass before merging
- Current status: 52 tests passing (23 domain + 7 validation + 14 integration + 8 auth)

## File Naming Conventions
- Java: PascalCase for classes, camelCase for methods
- TypeScript: PascalCase for components/types, camelCase for functions/variables
- Test files: `*Test.java` for unit tests, `*IntegrationTest.java` for integration tests

## Dependencies
- Backend: Spring Boot 3.2.0, Java 17, PostgreSQL, JJWT 0.12.3
- Frontend: Next.js 14, React 18, TypeScript 5.3.3, Tailwind CSS, Axios

